Generative / algorithmic art is an interesting medium. I was inspired to re-start doing this while at transmediale 2019, Berlin, thinking about the role of the creator in the process.

There needs to be an unsettling mix of precision and chaos, of symmetry and repetition, of the known and the irrelevant — aesthetically significant accidents. There is a lot of expression you can get through a generative medium, and this is what I try to explore.
